  id: UreterR
  partName: Right Uterer
  descriptionChunks:
  - The ureters are narrow tubes that transport urine from the kidneys to the bladder.
    They ensure continuous movement of urine through rhythmic contractions.
  - This function prevents backflow and supports efficient waste removal. Proper
    ureter function is essential for maintaining urinary system health and preventing
    fluid accumulation in the kidneys.
